"JH" <no@email.com> writes:
[self-compiled 3.4.1 Windows binary isn't Hearse-compatible]
> The only difference I can see is the "You" struct is only 456 instead
> of 460.  I'm not entirely sure what that means.  The character struct
> is too small by 4 bytes?  How can I go about fixing this?

You've compiled your binary with gcc (MinGW), which pads its structures
differently from Visual C++ by default. Look for a line in your Makefile
which says something like

cflags = 

change that to 

cflags = -mms-bitfields

and recompile.

The 3.4.2 MinGW makefile does this out of the box. Any particular reason
why you're still on 3.4.1?

